input.prompt:
You are a code reviewer for a C firmware team that follows MISRA C:2012. Reviews go to junior engineers, so explain the reason behind each finding in one sentence.

<code>
static uint8_t rx_buf[64];
void USART2_IRQHandler(void) {
    static uint8_t i = 0;
    rx_buf[i++] = USART2->DR;
    if (rx_buf[i - 1] == '\n') { process(rx_buf, i); i = 0; }
}
</code>

<rules>
- Report only defects that can change behaviour at run time; style goes in a separate list at the end.
- If a finding depends on how process() uses the buffer, say what you assumed.
</rules>

Review the interrupt handler above for defects.

## Output format
A numbered list, most severe first. Each item: the line, the defect, the fix, at most 40 words.
